1
00:00:00,066 --> 00:00:01,485
(This drama complied with production
guidelines for filming child actors,)

2
00:00:01,568 --> 00:00:03,003
(and some scenes used
generative AI technology.)

3
00:00:09,175 --> 00:00:11,277
(Episode 18)

4
00:00:11,378 --> 00:00:13,079
You're going to work dressed like that?

5
00:00:14,514 --> 00:00:16,316
Why? Does it look strange?

6
00:00:16,449 --> 00:00:17,634
Is your office a school?

7
00:00:17,717 --> 00:00:20,304
A ratty T-shirt and jeans, really?
Honestly, this girl,

8
00:00:20,387 --> 00:00:21,888
how do you know so little?

9
00:00:22,155 --> 00:00:23,674
Mom, come on...

10
00:00:23,757 --> 00:00:26,243
It's not like I work
in the Yeouido finance district.

11
00:00:26,326 --> 00:00:28,011
- We just...
- Enough.

12
00:00:28,094 --> 00:00:29,313
Go change right now.

13
00:00:29,396 --> 00:00:32,883
A grown adult who can't tell work clothes
from clothes for meeting friends?

14
00:00:32,966 --> 00:00:34,701
Like a child who was never taught a thing?

15
00:00:35,235 --> 00:00:37,187
A suit is even more uncomfortable!

16
00:00:37,270 --> 00:00:38,555
How am I supposed to work in that?

17
00:00:38,638 --> 00:00:40,624
Then at least throw on a jacket.
And change your pants.

18
00:00:40,707 --> 00:00:42,842
That means changing everything.

19
00:00:43,810 --> 00:00:45,128
Does it look that bad?

20
00:00:45,211 --> 00:00:46,463
Do I really have to wear a suit?

21
00:00:46,546 --> 00:00:49,449
Even if it's not a suit,
dress close to one.

22
00:00:49,616 --> 00:00:51,718
How does your CEO come to work?

23
00:00:54,154 --> 00:00:56,556
- He was wearing a suit.
- There's your answer.

24
00:00:56,956 --> 00:00:58,224
I'm done arguing.

25
00:01:01,127 --> 00:01:03,229
Good grief...

26
00:01:03,763 --> 00:01:05,899
Getting a job, of all things...

27
00:01:08,468 --> 00:01:10,003
He hasn't called lately, has he?

28
00:01:10,570 --> 00:01:12,839
That boy. O Reum, or whatever his name is.

29
00:01:13,540 --> 00:01:16,076
- No.
- Don't you start guarding me too.

30
00:01:16,476 --> 00:01:19,596
I lost years standing guard
in case your dad snuck off to Seo Chon,

31
00:01:19,679 --> 00:01:21,465
and now I have to keep an eye
on my daughter too?

32
00:01:21,548 --> 00:01:24,951
So just drop it. Seriously.

33
00:01:25,752 --> 00:01:27,754
Earn good money and take care of me.

34
00:01:30,623 --> 00:01:33,026
I'll earn good money and move out.

35
00:01:33,626 --> 00:01:35,161
That girl...

36
00:01:51,811 --> 00:01:55,215
Dad, I think I've met some good people.

37
00:01:55,582 --> 00:01:57,283
I'm going to give it my all.

38
00:02:05,158 --> 00:02:07,927
There really are more animals than people.

39
00:02:08,528 --> 00:02:10,930
The colors are better
than in the older books.

40
00:02:11,397 --> 00:02:12,616
But...

41
00:02:12,699 --> 00:02:15,668
Boss, I had no idea
you had a dream like this.

42
00:02:16,736 --> 00:02:19,439
This isn't the café,
so don't call me boss.

43
00:02:19,672 --> 00:02:23,576
If people overhear,
they'll think the company is mine.

44
00:02:23,810 --> 00:02:26,412
- That's unfair to the CEO.
- Then what should I call you?

45
00:02:26,613 --> 00:02:29,249
- Just Tae O?
- That's even worse.

46
00:02:29,916 --> 00:02:31,735
I should ask the CEO about it later.

47
00:02:31,818 --> 00:02:34,554
I'll ask to be made director, like Ji Hu.

48
00:02:35,655 --> 00:02:37,023
Director.

49
00:02:37,123 --> 00:02:38,825
That actually sounds kind of cool.

50
00:02:41,060 --> 00:02:43,096
You should ask for manager. Manager Na.

51
00:02:43,463 --> 00:02:45,031
- Manager Na?
- Director, then.

52
00:02:52,539 --> 00:02:53,740
Father, you haven't left yet?

53
00:02:54,140 --> 00:02:55,975
I just got back from a breakfast meeting.

54
00:02:57,977 --> 00:02:59,345
Aren't you running late?

55
00:03:00,280 --> 00:03:02,265
My employees are already
at the office working.

56
00:03:02,348 --> 00:03:04,034
We're heading straight
to the exhibition hall today.

57
00:03:04,117 --> 00:03:06,286
- Want a ride?
- Thank you.

58
00:03:06,419 --> 00:03:07,419
You rascal!

59
00:03:14,527 --> 00:03:16,429
You want to leave it blank?

60
00:03:17,964 --> 00:03:21,668
So kids can fill it in
and create their own stories?

61
00:03:22,569 --> 00:03:24,221
Doesn't that sound like so much fun?

62
00:03:24,304 --> 00:03:27,807
Then one single book could become
any number of different stories.

63
00:03:28,007 --> 00:03:30,376
They could even change the main character.

64
00:03:31,177 --> 00:03:33,730
And so kids can imagine and dress them up,

65
00:03:33,813 --> 00:03:35,448
I want to include cut-out pieces, too.

66
00:03:35,582 --> 00:03:39,819
Then we give the add-ons away at first
and get them to buy later.

67
00:03:41,321 --> 00:03:44,924
Making a tablet edition to sell
would be perfect.

68
00:03:45,091 --> 00:03:49,629
I don't know much about sales,
but it's possible, right?

69
00:03:49,929 --> 00:03:53,633
We took his investment,
so we owe him his money back.

70
00:03:54,767 --> 00:03:56,002
Knock, knock.

71
00:03:57,036 --> 00:03:59,839
How's the meeting going, everyone?

72
00:04:00,006 --> 00:04:02,542
- Yes.
- Uncle... I mean, sir.

73
00:04:02,775 --> 00:04:05,896
Looks like you've hired
an idea machine now.

74
00:04:05,979 --> 00:04:10,550
- Let's see what you've got.
- Really? What's for lunch?

75
00:04:10,683 --> 00:04:13,519
We're in the middle of a meeting,
and all you ask about is lunch?

76
00:04:13,620 --> 00:04:14,654
Then what?

77
00:04:14,754 --> 00:04:16,106
For starters,

78
00:04:16,189 --> 00:04:19,525
our job titles, and with vacation season
here, where we'll take our summer break,

79
00:04:19,626 --> 00:04:21,611
and how vacation time works,

80
00:04:21,694 --> 00:04:24,614
you've got a lot to tell us, sir.

81
00:04:24,697 --> 00:04:26,799
Vacation time...

82
00:04:27,734 --> 00:04:28,919
Didn't I tell you?

83
00:04:29,002 --> 00:04:30,921
You get personal days after three years,

84
00:04:31,004 --> 00:04:34,207
and paid vacation after five years.

85
00:04:34,574 --> 00:04:35,942
But if you don't like it, quit.

86
00:04:37,744 --> 00:04:39,078
In exchange,

87
00:04:39,312 --> 00:04:41,681
the break room is going up today.

88
00:04:42,015 --> 00:04:43,116
Anyone have anything to say?

89
00:04:47,020 --> 00:04:50,657
Sir! You keep startling us...

90
00:04:51,491 --> 00:04:54,594
Our leave policy is written right here.

91
00:04:54,894 --> 00:04:56,613
So why bring up nonsense?

92
00:04:56,696 --> 00:04:59,666
- What do you want for lunch?
- I'd like sushi.

93
00:05:00,033 --> 00:05:02,052
You're asking for it.

94
00:05:02,135 --> 00:05:04,904
- You're here?
- Work seems to be going well.

95
00:05:05,104 --> 00:05:08,975
This is the talent I told you about,
from "The Captain's Library Publishing."

96
00:05:11,044 --> 00:05:14,180
Hello. It's a pleasure to meet you.
My name is Na Ji Ni.

97
00:05:15,181 --> 00:05:17,650
Ji Ni? Like a genie in a lamp?

98
00:05:19,385 --> 00:05:21,271
No, not quite...

99
00:05:21,354 --> 00:05:24,957
It's a pure Korean name that means
to live carrying many gifts.

100
00:05:26,759 --> 00:05:28,278
You graduated
from Hanguk University's art school,

101
00:05:28,361 --> 00:05:31,464
and you're just making children's books?
Isn't that a waste?

102
00:05:31,664 --> 00:05:33,833
That's why I'm paying her well.

103
00:05:35,335 --> 00:05:38,255
I've loved storybooks since I was little.

104
00:05:38,338 --> 00:05:41,708
I'm truly grateful
for this wonderful opportunity.

105
00:05:43,509 --> 00:05:46,229
Did I interrupt your meeting?

106
00:05:46,312 --> 00:05:49,015
We're ordering lunch. Join us.

107
00:05:49,615 --> 00:05:51,568
But it's been so long, Auntie,

108
00:05:51,651 --> 00:05:53,052
shouldn't you say,
"Tae O, it's been ages!"

109
00:05:53,152 --> 00:05:56,189
"You've gotten even more handsome?"
Something like that?

110
00:05:56,356 --> 00:05:58,958
Where'd you get all that nerve?

111
00:05:59,225 --> 00:06:00,710
Right after I graduated,

112
00:06:00,793 --> 00:06:04,063
I've been through it all,
working at cafés and in sales.

113
00:06:04,597 --> 00:06:06,332
But you,

114
00:06:06,632 --> 00:06:09,369
you've only gotten
more elegant and beautiful.

115
00:06:10,737 --> 00:06:12,455
Have I? Thank you.

116
00:06:12,538 --> 00:06:14,257
It's good to see you, Tae O.

117
00:06:14,340 --> 00:06:15,375
Thank you.

118
00:06:15,508 --> 00:06:16,459
Honey,

119
00:06:16,542 --> 00:06:19,445
- can I catch a movie at the Cine Mall?
- Of course.

120
00:06:20,480 --> 00:06:21,481
It was lovely meeting you.

121
00:06:30,390 --> 00:06:32,392
- That threw you, didn't it?
- A little.

122
00:06:33,292 --> 00:06:35,612
But I'm used to it.
My mom's pretty tough too.

123
00:06:35,695 --> 00:06:40,266
True. Even when she stopped by the café,
she never really relaxed on the couch.

124
00:06:40,566 --> 00:06:42,118
Always with her back straight.

125
00:06:42,201 --> 00:06:43,687
You notice the strangest things.

126
00:06:43,770 --> 00:06:47,206
I told you. You see a lot
when you run a business.

127
00:06:47,540 --> 00:06:50,209
- What should we eat?
- I'm not hungry...

128
00:06:51,444 --> 00:06:55,114
Figures. Jung A would order everything
before I even said a word...

129
00:06:55,848 --> 00:06:58,418
- She's something else...
- Jeon Jung A...

130
00:07:02,021 --> 00:07:03,956
I said I'm going to Na Ji Ni.

131
00:07:05,291 --> 00:07:07,026
I'll go and beg her.

132
00:07:07,460 --> 00:07:09,579
- I'll plead with her.
- Mai!

133
00:07:09,662 --> 00:07:11,264
Let's give it a little time.

134
00:07:11,431 --> 00:07:14,400
How can we wait?
He's fading right in front of us.

135
00:07:16,302 --> 00:07:17,687
He's on nothing but an IV drip.

136
00:07:17,770 --> 00:07:19,939
He can't eat a single thing right now.

137
00:07:20,039 --> 00:07:22,942
No one is as desperate as I am.

138
00:07:23,176 --> 00:07:25,044
Not you, not your mother.

139
00:07:25,178 --> 00:07:26,212
You're both being cruel.

140
00:07:26,345 --> 00:07:28,498
There's no guarantee she'll
be a bone marrow match.

141
00:07:28,581 --> 00:07:30,400
There's no guarantee she won't be, either.

142
00:07:30,483 --> 00:07:32,202
That's exactly why I said I'd go.

143
00:07:32,285 --> 00:07:34,270
Her mother told us
never to contact them again.

144
00:07:34,353 --> 00:07:36,673
So we just sit here like this?

145
00:07:36,756 --> 00:07:38,208
I'm losing my mind too.

146
00:07:38,291 --> 00:07:40,543
This is too cruel.

147
00:07:40,626 --> 00:07:43,162
Is your pride really worth this much?

148
00:07:45,331 --> 00:07:47,033
It isn't pride.

149
00:08:05,218 --> 00:08:07,086
I'll go.

150
00:08:08,988 --> 00:08:10,656
And what will you do when you get there?

151
00:08:10,823 --> 00:08:14,144
She blames you for that girl's hurt arm,
and you want to walk in there?

152
00:08:14,227 --> 00:08:17,063
I still have to beg. Mai is right.

153
00:08:17,597 --> 00:08:19,298
She just might be a match.

154
00:08:20,399 --> 00:08:22,502
And if she is, would she even give it?

155
00:08:23,035 --> 00:08:25,238
In her place, I wouldn't hear a word.

156
00:08:25,571 --> 00:08:28,307
Still, we can't just sit back
and do nothing.

157
00:08:28,708 --> 00:08:30,977
Don't worry about it.
Just do your job at the station.

158
00:08:31,277 --> 00:08:32,879
And don't get on their bad side again.

159
00:08:33,613 --> 00:08:35,181
When do you go to work?

160
00:08:36,983 --> 00:08:39,519
- I want to resign.
- Have you lost your mind?

161
00:08:42,522 --> 00:08:45,024
- Mom!
- How can you say that right now?

162
00:08:45,391 --> 00:08:47,727
At least one of us
needs to hold it together.

163
00:08:47,960 --> 00:08:50,930
Do I look like I have it easy?
Want to add one more burden?

164
00:08:51,063 --> 00:08:53,616
Did they tell you to go?
Did Director Choi ask you to resign?

165
00:08:53,699 --> 00:08:56,969
- No, that's not it...
- Should I go see him?

166
00:08:57,103 --> 00:09:00,039
What am I, a high schooler?

167
00:09:00,373 --> 00:09:02,192
I know Director Choi a little myself.

168
00:09:02,275 --> 00:09:04,377
He was the emcee at my wedding.

169
00:09:09,849 --> 00:09:11,717
Yeong Ju!

170
00:09:12,685 --> 00:09:15,087
Don't worry about me. I'll handle it.

171
00:09:15,354 --> 00:09:18,357
Fine. Please do handle it. Please.

172
00:09:20,293 --> 00:09:21,594
Yeong Ju!

173
00:09:23,596 --> 00:09:25,231
I said I heard you.

174
00:09:26,232 --> 00:09:27,900
Yeong Ju!

175
00:09:35,041 --> 00:09:36,275
Let's go.

176
00:09:50,189 --> 00:09:51,490
Mrs. No.

177
00:09:52,358 --> 00:09:53,893
- Yes?
- You haven't left yet?

178
00:09:54,594 --> 00:09:57,597
I was just about to. Why?

179
00:09:58,864 --> 00:10:01,718
I meant to give you this earlier,
but it slipped my mind...

180
00:10:01,801 --> 00:10:04,921
I was deciding whether to bring it
to your home or to the hospital...

181
00:10:05,004 --> 00:10:06,405
And here you still are.

182
00:10:06,539 --> 00:10:08,224
What is this now?

183
00:10:08,307 --> 00:10:11,277
I only ever take from you.
It's too much.

184
00:10:11,377 --> 00:10:12,878
It's nothing much.

185
00:10:13,212 --> 00:10:15,314
The child can barely eat anything now.

186
00:10:15,414 --> 00:10:19,018
An adult could force it down,
but a child can't.

187
00:10:20,219 --> 00:10:22,288
Try giving him this.

188
00:10:22,622 --> 00:10:24,590
If I had to give it a name,

189
00:10:24,857 --> 00:10:26,726
herbal tonic syrup for children.

190
00:10:26,826 --> 00:10:28,928
I made it and named it myself.

191
00:10:29,095 --> 00:10:31,597
Either way, it should help a little.

192
00:10:32,465 --> 00:10:34,533
Thank you. I can't refuse this.

193
00:10:34,700 --> 00:10:36,535
He really can't eat anything.

194
00:10:36,669 --> 00:10:40,272
You should go. If you're headed
to the hospital, shall I drive you?

195
00:10:41,107 --> 00:10:42,908
There's somewhere I have to go.

196
00:10:43,142 --> 00:10:45,745
I was gathering my courage for it.

197
00:10:46,212 --> 00:10:48,781
It's a place I dread going to.

198
00:10:49,515 --> 00:10:50,983
Where are you going?

199
00:10:53,519 --> 00:10:56,789
Do I look selfish to you?

200
00:10:57,123 --> 00:10:58,357
Who says that?

201
00:10:58,557 --> 00:11:00,192
My daughter-in-law.

202
00:11:00,426 --> 00:11:03,095
And my son seems to think so too.

203
00:11:03,663 --> 00:11:06,198
There are reasons for it, of course.

204
00:11:06,465 --> 00:11:07,633
But still...

205
00:11:07,767 --> 00:11:10,253
They don't seem to consider
my side of it at all,

206
00:11:10,336 --> 00:11:11,837
and that hurts.

207
00:11:12,438 --> 00:11:16,008
I don't know the details,
so I'm not sure what to say, but...

208
00:11:16,676 --> 00:11:18,428
From what I've seen of you,

209
00:11:18,511 --> 00:11:21,447
you're anything but selfish.

210
00:11:24,183 --> 00:11:27,219
Thank you for making this.
I'll make sure he takes it.

211
00:11:28,287 --> 00:11:30,840
You need to find a donor soon...

212
00:11:30,923 --> 00:11:34,360
Chemotherapy is harsh,
and it'll be hard on a child.

213
00:11:35,661 --> 00:11:36,762
I know.

214
00:11:52,378 --> 00:11:54,013
Father.

215
00:11:54,146 --> 00:11:56,048
I've come here again,

216
00:11:56,515 --> 00:11:58,384
to the apartment he lived in.

217
00:11:59,218 --> 00:12:02,054
I thought I'd never have reason to come...

218
00:12:02,521 --> 00:12:04,557
I came because of O Reum.

219
00:12:05,291 --> 00:12:07,393
So that I can find the right words,

220
00:12:07,927 --> 00:12:09,695
please help me.

221
00:12:17,870 --> 00:12:18,938
Yeong Ju?

222
00:12:23,943 --> 00:12:25,811
So you actually came.

223
00:12:28,814 --> 00:12:32,284
This is the home where he and I lived.

224
00:12:33,285 --> 00:12:37,490
- I know.
- What, are you here to evict us?

225
00:12:38,057 --> 00:12:40,025
I thought that was settled.

226
00:13:10,322 --> 00:13:15,528
He loved taking photos.
You know that. Sit down.

227
00:13:26,205 --> 00:13:28,674
We could've just talked outside.

228
00:13:28,908 --> 00:13:32,144
I have to cook dinner. Ji Ni got a job.

229
00:13:33,179 --> 00:13:36,499
- A job?
- Once I quit the orchestra and lessons,

230
00:13:36,582 --> 00:13:38,250
she must have felt guilty.

231
00:13:39,018 --> 00:13:42,772
The credit card bills are bad enough,
thanks to someone, plus the mortgage too.

232
00:13:42,855 --> 00:13:45,558
And I don't have two sons earning for me.

233
00:13:46,826 --> 00:13:48,527
I see.

234
00:13:48,894 --> 00:13:51,630
What on earth brings you all the way here?

235
00:13:52,298 --> 00:13:55,334
- I have a favor to ask.
- I knew it.

236
00:13:55,634 --> 00:13:58,070
You'd never set foot here
unless you wanted something.

237
00:13:58,337 --> 00:13:59,605
That's true.

238
00:14:01,907 --> 00:14:07,213
Our O Reum has blood cancer...

239
00:14:08,214 --> 00:14:11,650
- He needs a bone marrow transplant.
- Really?

240
00:14:11,951 --> 00:14:16,722
Chemotherapy isn't enough?
That's terrible...

241
00:14:17,656 --> 00:14:22,194
But no one in our family is a match.

242
00:14:22,595 --> 00:14:26,899
No one on his mother's side
in Vietnam is a match.

243
00:14:28,367 --> 00:14:31,437
- And?
- Well...

244
00:14:33,906 --> 00:14:37,343
- Ji Ni is the only...
- Have you lost your mind?

245
00:14:38,210 --> 00:14:41,914
I'm begging you.
Couldn't she just get tested once?

246
00:14:42,748 --> 00:14:44,483
We're searching overseas,

247
00:14:44,717 --> 00:14:46,385
but if this keeps dragging on,

248
00:14:46,852 --> 00:14:48,587
he won't be able to hold on,

249
00:14:48,821 --> 00:14:51,523
and I'm terrified
we'll end up losing him.

250
00:14:52,358 --> 00:14:54,159
He can't handle the chemo,

251
00:14:54,727 --> 00:14:57,863
he can't eat, and time
keeps slipping away...

252
00:14:58,097 --> 00:14:59,298
Get out!

253
00:15:00,065 --> 00:15:04,153
I can't hold my anger back.

254
00:15:04,236 --> 00:15:07,506
- Get out. Get out, I said!
- Please...

255
00:15:07,740 --> 00:15:10,226
Help us, and I'll never forget it.

256
00:15:10,309 --> 00:15:11,610
The nerve of you.

257
00:15:11,810 --> 00:15:14,546
I don't even know what to say.

258
00:15:14,780 --> 00:15:17,716
What would you have done
if I'd never had Ji Ni?

259
00:15:17,883 --> 00:15:20,753
Do you remember how you treated me
when I had Ji Ni?

260
00:15:21,287 --> 00:15:23,422
Have you forgotten? Is your memory going?

261
00:15:24,189 --> 00:15:25,675
I can't believe this.

262
00:15:25,758 --> 00:15:27,526
How dare you ask Ji Ni for anything?

263
00:15:27,793 --> 00:15:30,396
- This is not right!
- I know. I know all of it.

264
00:15:30,863 --> 00:15:32,932
I know exactly how you must feel.

265
00:15:33,165 --> 00:15:34,934
But I'm desperate.

266
00:15:35,334 --> 00:15:39,956
I never set foot here
even when you took my husband.

267
00:15:40,039 --> 00:15:43,075
I have no interest
in understanding that, so get out.

268
00:15:43,742 --> 00:15:46,612
I won't say another word. Unbelievable!

269
00:15:47,246 --> 00:15:49,748
Honey, your ex-wife is here,

270
00:15:49,882 --> 00:15:52,451
asking our daughter to get tested.
Unbelievable.

271
00:15:52,685 --> 00:15:54,520
Does any of that make sense?

272
00:15:54,720 --> 00:15:56,922
Get out! I said!

273
00:15:57,556 --> 00:15:58,824
Ji Ni!

274
00:16:01,460 --> 00:16:02,695
Ji Ni.

275
00:16:03,595 --> 00:16:04,897
What brings you all the way here?

276
00:16:05,064 --> 00:16:07,132
Go to your room.
This has nothing to do with you.

277
00:16:07,566 --> 00:16:08,834
I'm asking you.

278
00:16:09,668 --> 00:16:11,570
To see if your marrow matches O Reum's,

279
00:16:11,971 --> 00:16:13,806
couldn't you get tested just once?

280
00:16:13,939 --> 00:16:15,574
You adored O Reum too.

281
00:16:15,874 --> 00:16:17,676
Just this once. I'm begging you.

282
00:16:20,045 --> 00:16:21,847
I understand how painful this must be,

283
00:16:23,148 --> 00:16:24,750
but I still don't think this is right.

284
00:16:24,850 --> 00:16:26,919
Exactly! No, this isn't right.

285
00:16:27,086 --> 00:16:29,105
Leave, Yeong Ju. Get out!

286
00:16:29,188 --> 00:16:32,458
- Ji Ni...
- I said get out!

287
00:16:52,411 --> 00:16:53,946
Don't give it another thought.

288
00:16:54,079 --> 00:16:55,381
And don't you pity her either.

289
00:16:55,981 --> 00:17:00,236
When we were on our knees,
begging and pleading,

290
00:17:00,319 --> 00:17:02,554
they showed us no sympathy at all.

291
00:17:10,229 --> 00:17:13,599
Please, ma'am.
Please let me be Cha Ji Ni.

292
00:17:13,932 --> 00:17:17,503
I'm begging you. Please? Ma'am!

293
00:17:19,905 --> 00:17:22,474
Get lost. How dare you show up here?

294
00:17:22,574 --> 00:17:23,859
You should never have been born.

295
00:17:23,942 --> 00:17:25,744
You should've died in her womb.

296
00:17:28,614 --> 00:17:30,466
Get out! You filthy girl.

297
00:17:30,549 --> 00:17:32,584
- That's enough, Seung Woo.
- Tell her to leave.

298
00:17:37,256 --> 00:17:39,241
Just go. Don't ever come back.

299
00:17:39,324 --> 00:17:42,161
Go live like your mother.

300
00:17:43,796 --> 00:17:45,614
- Go!
- Ma'am!

301
00:17:45,697 --> 00:17:49,635
Ma'am, please wait!

302
00:17:49,735 --> 00:17:50,969
Ma'am!

303
00:18:24,336 --> 00:18:25,604
O Reum,

304
00:18:26,371 --> 00:18:27,873
what are we going to do?

305
00:18:28,974 --> 00:18:31,110
There's nothing I can do for you.

306
00:18:44,890 --> 00:18:48,460
O Reum! Please, just eat a little.

307
00:18:49,995 --> 00:18:51,230
O Reum.

308
00:18:54,366 --> 00:18:55,901
You can't do this.

309
00:18:57,870 --> 00:18:58,904
Seung Hyun.

310
00:19:11,517 --> 00:19:14,386
Now, where did our O Reum go?

311
00:19:16,054 --> 00:19:18,157
Here it comes, into O Reum's mouth.

312
00:19:18,524 --> 00:19:20,659
Off it goes.

313
00:19:24,296 --> 00:19:27,232
O Reum, want to go home with me?

314
00:19:29,401 --> 00:19:31,537
Three more spoonfuls and we'll go home.

315
00:19:31,837 --> 00:19:35,174
- I'll carry you on my back.
- Tell the drawing lady to come too.

316
00:19:35,507 --> 00:19:36,909
The drawing lady?

317
00:19:38,744 --> 00:19:41,847
All right. I'll call her. Let's eat first.

318
00:19:47,019 --> 00:19:48,620
That's my boy.

319
00:20:12,211 --> 00:20:13,278
Goodness!

320
00:20:15,414 --> 00:20:16,882
You scared me.

321
00:20:23,722 --> 00:20:25,157
Where have you been?

322
00:20:25,290 --> 00:20:27,326
Why so formal? You're scaring me.

323
00:20:28,560 --> 00:20:30,028
Why aren't you at the hospital?

324
00:20:30,596 --> 00:20:31,863
Mother,

325
00:20:32,631 --> 00:20:34,266
come with me to their home.

326
00:20:35,033 --> 00:20:36,268
Is that why you came?

327
00:20:37,869 --> 00:20:40,505
No one understands how I feel. No one.

328
00:20:41,340 --> 00:20:43,275
I do. Of course I do.

329
00:20:43,875 --> 00:20:46,178
O Reum isn't only your child.

330
00:20:46,378 --> 00:20:47,713
That's easy to say.

331
00:20:48,413 --> 00:20:51,516
If you truly meant that,
you couldn't do this.

332
00:20:53,518 --> 00:20:54,853
I just got back.

333
00:20:56,488 --> 00:20:57,689
Just now?

334
00:20:58,390 --> 00:20:59,591
You're coming from there?

335
00:21:00,959 --> 00:21:02,527
I clasped my hands and begged her.

336
00:21:03,095 --> 00:21:05,964
I pleaded with her
to at least get tested.

337
00:21:06,198 --> 00:21:07,850
What did she say? Will she do it?

338
00:21:07,933 --> 00:21:10,202
I don't know. She'll think it over.

339
00:21:10,402 --> 00:21:14,156
How can you not know?
You have to drag her here.

340
00:21:14,239 --> 00:21:17,175
I did everything I could.
Give me some credit.

341
00:21:17,509 --> 00:21:19,778
You are not the only one aching.

342
00:21:20,412 --> 00:21:21,880
Tell her we'll pay her.

343
00:21:23,148 --> 00:21:25,651
Tell her we'll pay whatever she wants.

344
00:21:26,785 --> 00:21:28,153
Let's wait.

345
00:21:28,520 --> 00:21:30,822
We can't drag her there by force.

346
00:21:30,989 --> 00:21:32,724
Mother...

347
00:21:34,626 --> 00:21:37,195
I know. I know it too.

348
00:21:47,039 --> 00:21:48,640
Hello.

349
00:21:49,341 --> 00:21:51,810
- You're eating late tonight.
- Come in, my future daughter-in-law.

350
00:21:51,910 --> 00:21:53,495
If you haven't eaten, join us.

351
00:21:53,578 --> 00:21:55,380
It's fine. I'll see Ji Hu first.

352
00:21:57,449 --> 00:22:00,018
- Father.
- Yes?

353
00:22:00,619 --> 00:22:02,538
My dad isn't feeling well.

354
00:22:02,621 --> 00:22:04,523
Is that so? Do you need to go?

355
00:22:04,723 --> 00:22:06,858
Yes. That's why I came to tell Ji Hu.

356
00:22:07,259 --> 00:22:08,527
I'm on a flight tomorrow morning.

357
00:22:09,261 --> 00:22:11,029
Forgive me, but is it his blood pressure?

358
00:22:11,330 --> 00:22:15,467
Yes. He took the medicine you gave him,
but it seems worse this time.

359
00:22:15,701 --> 00:22:17,736
All right. I understand.

360
00:22:21,473 --> 00:22:23,175
Do we have any medicine to spare?

361
00:22:23,675 --> 00:22:25,210
I'll go put some together for her.

362
00:22:25,944 --> 00:22:28,046
He's destined for big things. I'm worried.

363
00:22:28,246 --> 00:22:29,481
Madam,

364
00:22:30,315 --> 00:22:33,018
could this man of small things
have another bowl of rice?

365
00:22:34,386 --> 00:22:37,122
- You get stranger by the day.
- It's fun.

366
00:22:38,056 --> 00:22:40,892
- All those storybooks made you childish.
- You think so?

367
00:22:49,901 --> 00:22:50,969
Yes.

368
00:22:55,607 --> 00:22:57,142
Ji Hu.

369
00:22:57,909 --> 00:23:00,178
What brings you here?

370
00:23:01,446 --> 00:23:02,881
Ji Hu.

371
00:23:05,517 --> 00:23:06,618
What's wrong?

372
00:23:07,319 --> 00:23:08,887
My dad isn't well.

373
00:23:09,121 --> 00:23:10,322
What?

374
00:23:10,589 --> 00:23:12,324
- How bad is it?
- He collapsed.

375
00:23:13,425 --> 00:23:15,260
I'm flying to my mom tomorrow.

376
00:23:15,360 --> 00:23:17,095
She called me in tears.

377
00:23:17,829 --> 00:23:18,964
I see.

378
00:23:21,066 --> 00:23:22,200
Have a safe trip.

379
00:23:24,836 --> 00:23:26,471
Can't you come with me?

380
00:23:27,472 --> 00:23:29,040
I have work here.

381
00:23:32,778 --> 00:23:33,912
Sit down.

382
00:23:37,382 --> 00:23:40,352
- What is it?
- You're not the same lately.

383
00:23:40,819 --> 00:23:43,522
- Work has just been busy.
- Even so.

384
00:23:43,889 --> 00:23:45,824
I feel so lonely and hurt.

385
00:23:46,691 --> 00:23:48,727
- It's because of Na Ji Ni, isn't it?
- No.

386
00:23:48,894 --> 00:23:51,013
Stop feeling inferior to Ji Ni.
You are you.

387
00:23:51,096 --> 00:23:52,664
I don't feel inferior.

388
00:23:53,098 --> 00:23:54,900
Ji Ni is the one who feels inferior to me.

389
00:23:56,168 --> 00:23:57,302
Yes?

390
00:23:58,470 --> 00:24:01,106
Take this to your father.

391
00:24:01,373 --> 00:24:03,475
I found some blood pressure pills at home.

392
00:24:03,575 --> 00:24:05,677
Tell him to take these,
not the ones I gave before.

393
00:24:06,511 --> 00:24:08,647
Yes. Thank you so much.

394
00:24:08,947 --> 00:24:12,117
He's like family to us. Of course.

395
00:24:13,485 --> 00:24:14,553
Get some rest.

396
00:24:19,691 --> 00:24:21,092
He's truly a good person.

397
00:24:22,794 --> 00:24:25,130
- Should I drive you home?
- You're sending me off already?

398
00:24:25,797 --> 00:24:27,132
We won't see each other for days.

399
00:24:28,233 --> 00:24:30,135
Are you really going to keep this up?

400
00:24:30,936 --> 00:24:33,371
You really have changed.

401
00:24:34,372 --> 00:24:35,841
I haven't.

402
00:24:36,908 --> 00:24:38,343
What about dinner?

403
00:24:38,910 --> 00:24:41,446
Let's go out. Anything you want?

404
00:24:41,947 --> 00:24:43,482
Forget dinner,

405
00:24:43,615 --> 00:24:45,134
let's have red bean porridge at Hotel M.

406
00:24:45,217 --> 00:24:47,169
Red bean porridge? You don't even eat it.

407
00:24:47,252 --> 00:24:49,371
They renovated it. It's supposed
to be gorgeous now.

408
00:24:49,454 --> 00:24:51,256
- Fully Japanese style.
- For the photos?

409
00:24:51,957 --> 00:24:53,725
I'm the only one who hasn't posted yet.

410
00:24:54,593 --> 00:24:56,345
If I wait until after England,
I'll fall even further behind.

411
00:24:56,428 --> 00:24:57,829
I want to post before I go.

412
00:24:59,364 --> 00:25:00,632
Let's hurry!

413
00:25:01,233 --> 00:25:02,901
Come on.

414
00:25:03,802 --> 00:25:05,103
All right.

415
00:25:16,214 --> 00:25:17,516
You went out?

416
00:25:18,550 --> 00:25:20,218
Uncle, have some red bean porridge.

417
00:25:21,786 --> 00:25:23,021
Why red bean porridge?

418
00:25:23,288 --> 00:25:24,856
Is that why you went out?

419
00:25:25,690 --> 00:25:28,226
Uncle, can love change too?

420
00:25:29,528 --> 00:25:31,663
How would I know? I've never been in love.

421
00:25:41,640 --> 00:25:42,874
What is it?

422
00:25:45,911 --> 00:25:49,314
How much can you forgive
when someone you love has lied?

423
00:25:49,981 --> 00:25:52,684
- Get some sleep.
- Uncle, talk to me.

424
00:25:54,719 --> 00:25:57,105
Love is love, and a lie is a lie.

425
00:25:57,188 --> 00:25:58,456
How can you mix the two?

426
00:25:59,591 --> 00:26:02,661
"Love is love, and a lie is a lie?"

427
00:26:02,794 --> 00:26:05,530
Saying you lied because you loved someone,

428
00:26:06,031 --> 00:26:08,366
I think the whole thing is a lie.

429
00:26:08,700 --> 00:26:10,302
If you're asking me, that's how I see it.

430
00:26:11,336 --> 00:26:12,504
I feel the same.

431
00:26:17,442 --> 00:26:18,443
Get some rest.

432
00:26:22,547 --> 00:26:23,548
What was that?

433
00:26:50,475 --> 00:26:52,644
Sorry. Did you wait long?

434
00:26:53,211 --> 00:26:54,346
- Not at all.
- Sit down.

435
00:26:54,746 --> 00:26:55,747
Yes.

436
00:26:56,648 --> 00:26:57,682
So what's going on?

437
00:26:58,049 --> 00:27:00,251
I hear you got a job.

438
00:27:00,685 --> 00:27:01,770
How did you know?

439
00:27:01,853 --> 00:27:04,222
I care about you.

440
00:27:05,757 --> 00:27:07,626
I made a promise to your father, too.

441
00:27:08,226 --> 00:27:10,862
If anything ever happened,
I'd look out for you first.

442
00:27:11,596 --> 00:27:12,864
Thank you.

443
00:27:14,432 --> 00:27:17,519
I just slipped out during my lunch break.

444
00:27:17,602 --> 00:27:19,871
Right, sorry. Go ahead.

445
00:27:50,502 --> 00:27:53,822
(Family Register)

446
00:27:53,905 --> 00:27:55,257
This has to stay a secret. No matter what.

447
00:27:55,340 --> 00:27:57,175
That child feels just like me.

448
00:27:57,275 --> 00:28:00,295
Sa Bin, what if we'd met at 20?

449
00:28:00,378 --> 00:28:02,030
You've got to have something to hope for.

450
00:28:02,113 --> 00:28:03,966
He'll be just fine
after breaking you like this.

451
00:28:04,049 --> 00:28:06,602
I can't breathe
until I go grab her by the hair.

452
00:28:06,685 --> 00:28:08,804
- If I got a divorce, would you take me?
- Are you serious?

453
00:28:08,887 --> 00:28:10,889
- Does it sound like a lie?
- If you came to me divorced,

454
00:28:11,623 --> 00:28:12,857
I'd take you.

455
00:28:15,894 --> 00:28:17,862
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
